<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45521" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">strătēgus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατηγός</span>.
		* <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a military
			leader</i>, <i>general</i>, <i>commander</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec strategus, nec tyrannus quisquam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Curc. 2, 3, 6</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the presider</i>,
				<i>president</i> at a banquet: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">strategum te facio huic convivio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Stich. 5, 4, 20</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 4, 23</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>